# Agent authoring

This rule applies only while creating or editing files under `agents/`.

## New agents

Copy `agents/_agent_template.md` to `agents/<name>/<name>.md` (no leading
underscore). Fill every template section before merge. Do not invent a
different heading set or omit the JSON output schema.

Required headings, in this order:

1. Charter
2. I/O contract
3. Definition of done
4. Tools / privileges
5. Anti-reward-hacking
6. Blocked protocol
7. Context acquisition
8. Repo conventions
9. Working style
10. Agent-specific guidance
11. Output schema

Frontmatter must parse as an agent: `name` equals the file stem, `description`
is non-empty and has no `<` / `>`, and only allowed keys are present
(`name`, `description`, `model`, `readonly`, `is_background`, `tools`,
`metadata`).

## Imported agents

Adapt every imported or third-party agent to this template before merge.
Keep specialty instructions under **Agent-specific guidance**. Rewrite
frontmatter, I/O contract, anti-reward-hacking, blocked protocol, and
output schema so they match the template. Do not vendor a foreign heading
layout or a prose-only agent.

## Not an agent

Files whose names start with `_` (including `_agent_template.md`) are
templates or notes. Markdown under `evals/` is eval infrastructure.
Do not add either to a loadout `agents:` list, do not sync them to
`.claude/agents/`, and do not treat them as dispatchable subagents.
